{"id": "EUVD-2026-59394", "enisaUuid": "1f11b6a5-4ea5-3eef-affa-1724affdc8e4", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/bnxt_re: Avoid repeated requests to allocate WC pages\n\nApplications can request multiple WC pages for the same ucontext.\nAs of now, only 1 WC page per ucontext is supported. Add a lock to\navoid concurrent access and a check to fail repeated requests.\nAlso, if the mmap entry insert fails for the WC, free the Doorbell\npage index mapped for the WC page.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:57:28", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:45:04", "baseScore": 9.3, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8e59bd37d6d63a06ed452eaffe6c9d4ad903af7b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/00c71846874fea4917961236e49287a1850dcf98", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/478c4d24193fe3e6aa2accd4874ae43000e4a217", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/da406b8b49c1dfe661a497483940d7ee781430db", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/441baa79043431807115fd030d7d0bb14ed441a0"], "aliases": ["GHSA-3cmq-754m-66f5", "CVE-2026-72495"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "08e40868-1023-34a9-98f4-41b01d391db4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "360da60d6c6edb9740de7a8e6d8969d62ceff956 <8e59bd37d6d63a06ed452eaffe6c9d4ad903af7b"}, {"id": "24833a5d-9ef1-3d00-811a-26ebb4a30192", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "360da60d6c6edb9740de7a8e6d8969d62ceff956 <da406b8b49c1dfe661a497483940d7ee781430db"}, {"id": "2717de5a-7edd-3f55-808c-aad40e0857f1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "31dd50af-6bfe-3344-ac45-4f4e865a4980", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "3aa746e7-a396-3e53-a233-e17bba3fc536", "product": {"name": "L